Blackdrift: the app's Nimbus does not fetch experiments from Mozilla.

Why: the app's Nimbus (application-services) downloads experiment and rollout recipes from Mozilla's Remote
Settings collection "nimbus-mobile-experiments" (or "nimbus-preview") on
every launch, even though BuildConfig.NIMBUS_ENDPOINT is null. Blackdrift does
not take part in Mozilla experiments, and remote recipes could change app
behaviour without a Blackdrift release. Nimbus is given no server settings
(createNimbus() no longer takes the Remote Settings service), and
finishNimbusInitialization(), whose only job was fetchExperiments(), is
removed together with its call in FocusApplication.finishSetupMegazord().
Nimbus uses only the feature defaults compiled into nimbus.fml.yaml and the
bundled R.raw.initial_experiments. FocusNimbus feature lookups keep working.

This covers only the app side. GeckoView has its own Remote Settings
client, which downloaded Gecko's experiment and messaging collections
(nimbus-desktop-experiments and others) in the startup changesets bundle;
patch tree/0001-no-gecko-experiment-sync stops that. Remote Settings stays
on for its other collections (for example search configuration); see
blackdrift/README.md "Telemetry".

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

